# Wave W17-T (Route 131): moor rock — tower-isle rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: an ancient blue-grey shore rock, the Tempest Tower island\u2019s own stone standing in the corridor\u2019s water — old, weathered, unhurried; foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: Tempest Tower\u2019s island keeps the east — its shipped mouth cells and ancientpillar dressing stand byte-preserved; the rock kind carries the isle\u2019s register only). Route 131\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s only ancient blue-grey lane rock: split from Route 130\u2019s warm confluence rock by temperature and from Route 132\u2019s neutral channel-edge rock by age (weathered isle stone vs worked channel stone).
